{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And now go, lead the people</b> — For after I have relented from destroying them, you lead [them] toward that which I spoke to you: to the place of the Canaanite and the Amorite, etc. But He did not wish to mention this explicitly, for this is the way of anger, as if to say: what I spoke to you I will do for your honor, but I will not bear their sin, for <b>in the day of my visitation I will visit their sin upon them</b> — I will visit it upon them after they come into the land. This is a hint to the time when they will be exiled from it, or to what our Rabbis said (Sanhedrin 102a): there is no punishment that does not contain a measure of the sin of the Calf."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:20:26.328299534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}